%! Module defaults and private predicates.
%!
%! If @use does not set a parameter of the module, the parameter keeps its
%! default value. Predicates that are not outputs of the module are
%! private to it: a predicate with the same name in the using program is
%! a different predicate.
%!
%! The example shows:
%! - how a module parameter keeps its default value,
%! - how the predicates of a module stay private to it.

% $limit is not set, so it is 3, the default in hops.rls:
@use hops { edge = road } as routes .

road(a, b) .
road(b, c) .
road(c, d) .
road(d, e) .

% This is not the predicate hops of the module, which is private:
hops(local, value, 0) .

reachable(?x, ?y) :- routes::within(?x, ?y) .
localHops(?x, ?y, ?n) :- hops(?x, ?y, ?n) .

@output reachable, localHops .
